                        <summary>
                            
                            <p>This records a gift of five cows to the temple of Ūrbāgaṅkoṇḍaruḷiya-Nāyanār for the sacred <hi rend="italic">pañchagavya</hi> bath of the god by a certain Kāḷattināthaṉ a son of Kachchiyarāyar (or family ?) of Paruvūr.</p>						
                            
                            <p>Close to this is another inscription dated in the cyclic year Śubhakṛit (A.D. 1362-63 ?) which records a gift of two pieces of land measuring together 550 <hi rend="italic">kuḻi</hi> in extent, for a perpetual lamp in the temple, by one Tiruvēgambamuḍaiyān Tirumuḍikkāri of Śīdēvi village adjoining Śīkkāḍu by order of Goppaṇṇa-Uḍaiyar.</p>						
                            
                        </summary>
                    </msContents>
